  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\restriction:of{g(x__)}:on{X}]\nDeclares: f is \\function:on{X}:to{B}\nwhen:\n. g is \\function:on{A?}:to{B?}\n. X \\:set.theoretic.subset:/ A\nexpresses: f(x__) := g(x__)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"restriction of $g?$ on $X?$\"\n. written: \"g?\\big |_{X?}\"\n. description: \"The restriction $g|_X$ of a function $g : A \\rightarrow B$ to a\n                subset $X$ of $A$ is the function on $X$ that takes each input\n                to the same value $g$ does. It keeps the rule and shrinks the\n                domain.\"\nId: \"ea7eab01-792c-427f-91dc-a75f43513b38\"",
